{"duration": 49.98, "exact_word_timing": true, "lines": [{"beat": 0, "text": "A soldier punches twelve tiny dots into paper in the dead of night.", "start": 0.08, "end": 3.487}, {"beat": 1, "text": "His comrades laugh, saying the code is useless and too slow.", "start": 3.907, "end": 7.075}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Blind teen Louis Braille watches the demo at his school.", "start": 7.495, "end": 10.212}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He grabs the same slate and stylus.", "start": 10.432, "end": 12.329}, {"beat": 2, "text": "He spends months feeling each pattern.", "start": 12.549, "end": 14.332}, {"beat": 2, "text": "Then he halves the grid to three high and two wide.", "start": 14.552, "end": 17.012}, {"beat": 3, "text": "You see, it\u2019s like turning a bulky novel into a pocket\u2011size cheat sheet you can feel with one fingertip.", "start": 17.432, "end": 22.788}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Barbier\u2019s army night\u2011writing used twelve raised points to spell sounds, but soldiers could not master it.", "start": 23.208, "end": 28.982}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Braille cut the pattern in half, using only six dots to stand for letters, numbers and punctuation.", "start": 29.202, "end": 34.76}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Six dots sit comfortably under a single finger.", "start": 34.98, "end": 37.32}, {"beat": 4, "text": "A reader can feel a whole character in one quick touch.", "start": 37.54, "end": 40.211}, {"beat": 4, "text": "Writers can punch the dots faster than they could trace letters.", "start": 40.431, "end": 43.421}, {"beat": 5, "text": "Ironically, the system meant for soldiers became the world\u2019s universal language for the blind.", "start": 43.841, "end": 48.86}], "words": [{"w": "A", "start": 0.124, "end": 0.174, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "soldier", "start": 0.249, "end": 0.674, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "punches", "start": 0.724, "end": 1.074, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "twelve", "start": 1.149, "end": 1.424, "line": 0, "beat": 0}, {"w": "tiny", "start": 1.499,